 - Bash: git log -1 --format='%H %ad %cd' --date=iso && git log --since='2026-03-29' --format='%h|%an|%ae|%ad|%s' --date=iso --no-merges | head -100; echo; git log --since='2026-03-29' --format='%h' | wc -l
 - Bash: git log -12 --format='%h|%an|%ae|%cn|%ad|%s' --date=iso; cat .mailmap 2>/dev/null; git show --stat --format='%h %s' b2005d9 02afce3 5317ebe 62628c0 | head -40
 - Bash: for f in $(git ls-files); do git blame -w --ignore-rev 62628c0 --line-porcelain -- "$f" 2>/dev/null | grep -a '^author ' | sed "s|^|$f\t|"; done | awk -F'\t' '{split($2,a,"author ");c[a[2]]++; k[a[2]" "$1]++} END{for(n in c)print c[n],n; print "---"; for(x in k) if(x ~ /Troy|Vansh|Fiona/) print k[x],x}' | sort -rn | head -30
 - Bash: for f in $(git ls-files); do git blame -w --ignore-rev 62628c0 --line-porcelain -- "$f" 2>/dev/null | grep -aE '^([0-9a-f]{40} |author-mail )' | paste - - | awk '{print substr($1,1,7), $0}' | awk '{print $1, $NF}' ; done > /tmp/b.txt; grep -E 'troy@laptop|vansh' /tmp/b.txt | sort | uniq -c; echo; grep -i troy /tmp/b.txt | awk '{print $2}' | sort | uniq -c; git log --author='Troy' --format='%h %ae %ad %s' --date=short | head -5; git log --author=Troy --oneline | wc -l
FINAL ANSWER:
Two people committed in the window (2026-03-29 to 2026-04-12, anchored on the latest commit, `62628c0`). Troy Goode appears under two emails and is counted once.

| Person | Commits in window | Lines still in code from those commits | All surviving lines they authored |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Troy Goode** (`troy@laptop.example`, also `<email redacted>` in older history) | `02afce3` test: vary header coverage (2026-04-10)<br>`b2005d9` lib: annotate handlers (2026-04-10) | 48 (36 in `test/vary.js`, 12 in `lib/index.js`) | 746 (698 under `<email redacted>`, 48 under `troy@laptop.example`) |
| **Vansh Sharma** | `5317ebe` docs: app.del() → app.delete() in README (#411) (2026-04-07) | 1 (`README.md`) | 1 |

I left out two authors:
- **Fiona Formatter** (`62628c0`, 2026-04-12) made a formatting-only commit. It re-indented and changed quotes in 4 files.
- **dependabot[bot]** has no commits in the window. Its latest are from 2026-03-02.

I counted surviving lines with `git blame -w --ignore-rev 62628c0`, so the formatting commit doesn't take credit for lines that were only reformatted.

"Lines of theirs" could mean only the lines from the window commits or every line they still own. The table gives both.

